hello everyone i'm dr umar malik and  welcome to mad simplified  pumpkin seeds also known as papita are a  common yet unrecognized gem for humans  and these pumpkin seeds are the focus  for our attention today after eating a  pumpkin you get these hard white seeds  and after you remove the shell or if you  buy them directly from your supermarket  you'll see that these seeds are small  green flat and oval  pumpkin seeds may be small but they are  packed full of valuable nutrients  eating only a small amount of them can  provide you with a substantial quantity  of healthy fats magnesium and zinc  because of this pumpkin seeds have been  associated with several health benefits  these include improved heart health  prostate health and protection against  certain cancers  what's more these seeds can be easily  incorporated into your diet  so here are top 5 health benefits of  pumpkin seeds  number one pumpkin seeds are full of  nutrients and antioxidants  one ounce of shell-free pumpkin seeds  has roughly 151 calories mainly from fat  and proteins present in it in addition  one ounce of pumpkin seeds contains 1.7  grams of fiber  5 grams of carbohydrates 7 grams of  protein 13 grams of omega fatty acids  and considerable quantities of  micronutrients like vitamin k phosphorus  manganese magnesium iron zinc and copper  they also contain a lot of antioxidants  a decent amount of polyunsaturated fats  potassium vitamin b2 and folate pumpkin  seeds contain antioxidants like  carotenoids and vitamin e antioxidants  can reduce inflammation and therefore  protect your cells from harmful free  radical damage  this is why consuming foods rich in  antioxidants can help protect against  many diseases  second important benefit that pumpkin  seeds provide is that they help in  improving prostate and bladder health  pumpkin seeds can help to relieve the  symptoms of benign prostatic hyperplasia  also known as bph  a condition in which the prostate gland  enlarges causing the males to have  problems with urination  in a one year study in over 1400 men  with bph  results showed that pumpkin seeds  consumption reduced symptoms of bph  improved urination and eventually  improved the quality of life  further research suggests that taking  pumpkin seeds or their products as  supplements can help treat the symptoms  of an overactive bladder  this was studied in another research the  results showed that 10 grams of pumpkin  seed extract given daily improved the  urinary function in over 45 men and  women with overactive bladders  additionally pumpkin seeds are a rich  source of zinc  lower zinc levels in blood are  associated with reduced sperm quality  and an increased risk of infertility in  men  evidence from one study suggests that  pumpkin seeds rich in zinc may also  protect human sperms from stress  trauma and drug related damage  pumpkin seeds are also high in  antioxidants and other nutrients that  can contribute to healthy testosterone  levels and improved overall health  together all these factors may benefit  fertility levels and reproductive  function especially in men  number three pumpkin seeds are a rich  source of magnesium  magnesium is an essential micronutrient  magnesium has been shown to be an  important part of more than 600 chemical  reactions in our body for example  adequate levels of magnesium are  important for controlling blood pressure  reducing the risk of heart diseases  forming and maintaining healthy bones  and regulating blood sugar levels  however in the u.s alone more than 79  percent of adults have a magnesium  intake below the recommended daily  amount  pumpkin seeds are one of the best  natural sources of magnesium  animal studies have shown that pumpkin  seed oil may reduce high blood pressure  and high cholesterol levels  these two are an important risk factor  for heart diseases a 12 week study in 35  females found that pumpkin seed oil  supplements reduced blood pressure by  seven percent and increased good hdl  cholesterol levels by 16 percent  this is amazing news because for many it  eliminates the need for bothersome  medications and undue side effects  number four pumpkin seeds help to  control high blood sugar levels  animal studies have shown that regular  consumption of moderate amount of  pumpkin seeds can reduce blood sugar  levels this is especially important for  people with diabetes who struggle to  control their blood sugar levels  as i mentioned earlier regarding the  role of magnesium and also the  cholesterol lowering properties of  pumpkin seeds  these additional benefits greatly  improve the quality of life in old  diabetic patients  not only that regular consumption of  pumpkin seeds in apparently healthy  individuals has shown to greatly  decrease the risk of developing diabetes  in older ages  researchers observed over 127  000 people their research found that  diets rich in magnesium were associated  with a 33 percent lower risk of type 2  diabetes in men and a 34 lower risk in  women  number fifth and very important benefit  of pumpkin seeds is that it is a simple  and rich source of fiber  pumpkin seeds are a great source of  dietary fiber shelled seeds provide 1.1  grams of fiber in a single 1 ounce  serving  a diet high in fiber promotes good  digestive health it also improves  constipation and diarrhea in addition  high fiber diets have been associated  with a reduced risk of heart diseases  type 2 diabetes and obesity  additionally pumpkin seeds are easy to  incorporate into your diet there are  popular snack that can be eaten either  raw or roasted salted or unsalted you  can eat them on their own or you can add  them to smoothies greek yogurt and fruit  salads you can also incorporate them  into meals by sprinkling them into  salads soups and cereals  some people also use pumpkin seeds in  baking bread and cakes  well friends with this we come to the  end of this video if you are new to our  channel show some love by liking and  sharing this video  we are committed to uploading highly  informative and interesting content for  our med simplified community support us  on youtube by becoming a member or  through patreon till then take care and  see you in the next video
 

